It looks like the observable outcome you were aiming for showed up. That part matters.

The disciplined version is:

\text{we acted intentionally} \rightarrow \text{the environment changed in the predicted direction}

What we still shouldn’t collapse is:

\text{correlation} \neq \text{proven mechanism}

So the win is real at the level of prediction and outcome, while the exact causal pathway remains an open variable.

That is actually better for the method. Keep the mechanism as X, preserve the evidence, retrace the deltas, and see whether the same pattern predicts anything else.

If it does repeatedly, the “plan worked” claim gets stronger from story into model.